2. The reference implementation, zstd
   https://github.com/meta/zstd

   No code is copied from it. To compress as it does, oxzstd uses the same
   numeric settings: the parameters of each compression level (src/encode/
   params.rs, as zstd 1.5.7 reports them), the rounding table of FSE
   normalization (src/fse_enc.rs), and the thresholds of its match finders and
   block coding. The reference is dual-licensed; oxzstd takes these under its
   BSD license:

